{"event": "report", "t": 1795222660.871, "claim": "fixed", "verdict": {"verdict": "fixed", "root_cause": {"category": "logic", "model": "rpt_category_performance", "summary": "The orders join was a LEFT JOIN, so 18 order lines whose order_id has no header in ORDERS (ORPHAN-ORD-* ids) survived with a NULL ordered_at. They formed a NULL sales_month bucket (4 rows, about $2,950.78 revenue, 31 units) in a report meant to be category by calendar month. Switching to INNER JOIN drops only lines that cannot be dated or tied to a real order."}, "evidence": [{"kind": "query", "ref": "rpt_category_performance grouped by sales_month", "finding": "Before the fix there was a NULL sales_month group with 4 rows and revenue 2950.7776. The view's revenue total (722313.24) equalled the total of all order lines, including those orphans."}, {"kind": "query", "ref": "stg_orders__order_lines left join stg_orders__orders on order_id", "finding": "18 order lines have order_id values like ORPHAN-ORD-*, with no matching row in stg_orders__orders. Their line_total sums to 2950.7776."}, {"kind": "query", "ref": "source reconciliation of model totals", "finding": "Revenue 719362.46 after the fix equals the sum of line_total over lines matched to orders. Gross profit (606094.05) and units (6559) match the same orphan-free population. Null sales_month rows are now 0, and the grain is category x month."}, {"kind": "lineage", "ref": "walk_lineage upstream", "finding": "The model reads only four staging views: stg_orders__orders, stg_orders__order_lines, stg_product__products and stg_product__product_variants. Grain checks show these are unique on their keys, so there is no fan-out from the other joins."}], "changes": [{"path": "models/marts/product/rpt_category_performance.sql", "summary": "Changed `left join orders o` to `inner join orders o` on order_id. Order lines without a valid order header can't be assigned a sales month and are excluded. Output columns, grain and materialization (view) are unchanged. Rebuilt with run_dbt rpt_category_performance+ (success)."}], "confidence": "medium"}, "diffs": [{"path": "models/marts/product/rpt_category_performance.sql", "diff": "--- a/models/marts/product/rpt_category_performance.sql\n+++ b/models/marts/product/rpt_category_performance.sql\n@@ -29,5 +29,5 @@\n from products p\n left join product_variants pv on p.product_id = pv.product_id\n left join order_lines ol on pv.variant_id = ol.variant_id\n-left join orders o on ol.order_id = o.order_id\n+inner join orders o on ol.order_id = o.order_id\n group by 1, 2\n"}], "text": "The verifier accepted the fix. The run is over.\n\n**Root cause:** `rpt_category_performance` joined `stg_orders__orders` with a LEFT JOIN. Eighteen order lines have `ORPHAN-ORD-*` order IDs with no matching order header. Those lines kept a NULL `ordered_at`, so they formed a NULL `sales_month` bucket: 4 rows, about $2,950.78 of revenue and 31 units. That bucket does not belong in a category-by-month report.\n\n**Change:** In `models/marts/product/rpt_category_performance.sql`, `left join orders o` became `inner join orders o`. Output columns, grain and the view materialization are unchanged. I rebuilt the model with `run_dbt` (`rpt_category_performance+`), and it succeeded.\n\n**Checks after the fix:**\n- The NULL `sales_month` rows are gone. All 198 rows have a month.\n- Revenue is $719,362.46, which equals the sum of `line_total` over order lines that match an order.\n- Units are 6,559, which is 6,590 less the 31 orphan units.\n- Gross profit is $606,094.05.\n\n**Confidence is medium.** I chose to drop the orphan lines rather than keep them in a separate bucket, and that is a business judgement. Whoever owns the report should confirm it. The verifier passed the fix.\n\n**Left alone:** `read_failure` also reports many failing staging tests and a seed collision on `product_categories` (a `PRODUCT_CATEGORIES` table already exists in `main`). Neither is in this model's lineage, so I did not touch them."}
